based on nylon 6/66 copolymer, adding 20% carbon fiber greatly enhances the strength, rigidity and toughness of nylon, and can replace metal materials in many occasions","source":"S-PEBA-eSUN-ePA-CF-Filament-TDS-V4-0","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Pitfalls and limitations","items":[{"id":"Q05038","text":"ePA-CF filament has strong rigidity and is not easy to bend.","source":"S-PEBA-eSUN-ePA-CF-Filament-TDS-V4-0","at":"p. 2","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Warping and shrinkage","items":[{"id":"Q05035","text":"High dimensional stability","source":"S-PEBA-eSUN-ePA-CF-Filament-TDS-V4-0","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q05036","text":"Low shrinkage, it is not easy to warp and crack when printing, and the surface of printed models is matte and delicate.","source":"S-PEBA-eSUN-ePA-CF-Filament-TDS-V4-0","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Surface finish","items":[{"id":"Q05037","text":"Matte surface effect","source":"S-PEBA-eSUN-ePA-CF-Filament-TDS-V4-0","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Moisture sensitivity","items":[{"id":"Q05039","text":"It is recommended to use them together with eBOX when printing.","source":"S-PEBA-eSUN-ePA-CF-Filament-TDS-V4-0","at":"p. 2","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Nozzle wear","items":[{"id":"Q05040","text":"ePA-CF is very easy to grind nozzles and extruder gears.","source":"S-PEBA-eSUN-ePA-CF-Filament-TDS-V4-0","at":"p. 2","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q05041","text":"It is recommended to use hardened steel nozzles or ruby nozzles.","source":"S-PEBA-eSUN-ePA-CF-Filament-TDS-V4-0","at":"p. 2","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q05042","text":"If possible, hardened steel extruder gears can be selected.","source":"S-PEBA-eSUN-ePA-CF-Filament-TDS-V4-0","at":"p. 2","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q05043","text":"If the printing time is long, the blockage will occur and the throat and nozzle need to be replaced.","source":"S-PEBA-eSUN-ePA-CF-Filament-TDS-V4-0","at":"p. 2","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Printing advice","items":[{"id":"Q05044","text":"In the feeding pipeline, excessive bending of filament should be avoided as much as possible.","source":"S-PEBA-eSUN-ePA-CF-Filament-TDS-V4-0","at":"p. 2","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q05045","text":"It is suggested to set skirt edge to better take the model from the forming bottom plate.","source":"S-PEBA-eSUN-ePA-CF-Filament-TDS-V4-0","at":"p. 2","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]}]},{"id":"G165-05","name":"Essentium PA-CF","maker":"Essentium","variant":null,"diameter":null,"twins":[],"composition":"a carbon fiber-infused polyamide filament specially formulated for additive manufacturing (p. 1, as the sheet states it); its safety data sheet names the polymer: \"Chemical characterization Polyamide (PA 6/66)\" (R-ESSENTIUM-INTAKE-20261020-b4959fb55a87, section 3), so it is filed under PA6/66-CF since 2026-10-20 (m490). The sheet states no fibre load.","certifications":null,"availability":null,"claim":null,"values":[{"key":"tensileModulusXY","id":"V014713","value":2.16,"mark":"counted","why":null,"annealed":null,"source":"R-ESSENTIUM-TDS-Essentium-PA-CF","page":1,"twin":null,"admitted":["moisture","treatment"],"at":"Tensile Modulus, GPa, Print Orientation XY"},{"key":"tensileModulusZ","id":"V014716","value":0.48,"mark":"counted","why":null,"annealed":null,"source":"R-ESSENTIUM-TDS-Essentium-PA-CF","page":1,"twin":null,"admitted":["moisture","treatment"],"at":"Tensile Modulus, GPa, Print Orientation ZX"},{"key":"tensileStrengthXY","id":"V014709","value":55.9,"mark":"counted