g-grade solution or open platform and even open-air printers.","source":"R-ESSENTIUM-TDS-Essentium-PA-CF","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q07265","text":"Excellent toughness","source":"R-ESSENTIUM-TDS-Essentium-PA-CF","at":"p. 2","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q07266","text":"High impact resistance","source":"R-ESSENTIUM-TDS-Essentium-PA-CF","at":"p. 2","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q07267","text":"Optimized for high flow","source":"R-ESSENTIUM-TDS-Essentium-PA-CF","at":"p. 2","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Moisture sensitivity","items":[{"id":"Q07259","text":"It is important to note, the mechanical properties of PA may change with water uptake as this material is moisture sensitive.","source":"R-ESSENTIUM-TDS-Essentium-PA-CF","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q07261","text":"Essentium PA-CF is an extremely hygroscopic thermoplastic and will absorb moisture from humid air.","source":"R-ESSENTIUM-TDS-Essentium-PA-CF","at":"p. 2","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q07262","text":"Keep the material in the vacuum sealed packaging until you are ready to print with it.","source":"R-ESSENTIUM-TDS-Essentium-PA-CF","at":"p. 2","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q07263","text":"PA-CF filament should always be fed to the printer in a dry container and stored in a dry cabinet.","source":"R-ESSENTIUM-TDS-Essentium-PA-CF","at":"p. 2","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q07264","text":"If the material does absorb more than 500ppm moisture, it should be dried in a low dew point (< -40˚C) oven or vacuum oven at 100 – 120˚C for 4 – 8 hours.","source":"R-ESSENTIUM-TDS-Essentium-PA-CF","at":"p. 2","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Printing advice","items":[{"id":"Q07260","text":"The best prints with Essentium PA typically occur utilizing a glass bed and a bed adhesion solution, such as a PA-solvent liquid compound.","source":"R-ESSENTIUM-TDS-Essentium-PA-CF","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]}]}],"layers":[{"part":"tensileStrength","pairs":[{"id":"G156-01","name":"eSUN ePA CF","xy":84.05,"z":50.34,"annealed":false},{"id":"G165-05","name":"Essentium PA-CF","xy":55.9,"z":19.3,"annealed":false}],"unpaired":[]},{"part":"tensileModulus","pairs":[{"id":"G165-05","name":"Essentium PA-CF","xy":2.16,"z":0.48,"annealed":false}],"unpaired":[]},{"part":"elongation","pairs":[{"id":"G156-01","name":"eSUN ePA CF","xy":7.42,"z":11.5,"annealed":false},{"id":"G165-05","name":"Essentium PA-CF","xy":18,"z":22,"annealed":false}],"unpaired":[]},{"part":"flexuralStrength","pairs":[{"id":"G156-01","name":"eSUN ePA CF","xy":127.5,"z":54.9,"annealed":false}],"unpaired":[]},{"part":"flexuralModulus","pairs":[{"id":"G156-01","name":"eSUN ePA CF","xy":6.45544,"z":1.65725,"annealed":false}],"unpaired":[]}],"published":[{"property":"Fibre content","domain":"physical","unit":"%","products":1,"lo":20,"hi":20,"median":20,"values":[20]},{"property":"Melt mass-flow rate","domain":"physical","unit":"g/10 min","products":1,"lo":11.46,"hi":11.46,"median":11.46,"values":[11.46]},{"property":"Melting temperature","domain":"thermal","unit":"°C","products":1,"lo":192,"hi":192,"median":192,"values":[192]}],"environment":[],"guide":null,"resin":null,"sources":[{"id":"R-ESSENTIUM-TDS-Essentium-PA-CF","publisher":"Essentium / Nexa3D","title":"Essentium PA-CF Technical Data Sheet","date":"2020-05-28","read":"2026-09-17","kind":"Manufacturer TDS","url":"https://nexa3d.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/TDS-Essentium-PA-CF.pdf","revision":"Version 1.0","note":"Two-page technical data sheet hosted by the current brand owner (Nexa3D): mechanical properties by print orientation, melting point and heat deflection, handling 